From 9f3d46e272d4c61a334eb36a7610703d25088386 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:26:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 71/71] Client mods kept on the server: the relay lists them
 with hashes, clients ask, download what differs, verify, and restart

- relay.lua: on joining, a "mods" message with every mod and file (size, SHA-256); "modget" answers with base64 chunks of
  a file (read once and cached while it downloads, rate limited, names checked by the engine)
- clientmods.lua (client): compares the list with what is installed, per file. Same hash: nothing. Different hash: updated.
  Missing locally: new. Only local: deleted, and a mod the server dropped is removed. Asks the player only if something
  differs, downloads only those files, the engine writes each one only if its SHA-256 matches, then deletes what is gone
- player.lua: the confirmation window (counts of new, updated and removed files, download size; install and restart, or
  decline and leave) and the restart question; global.lua wires it in
- openmw-mp-server: openmw.modstore for its folder (--client-mods, default multiplayer/clientmods or next to the program)
- README: how a server hands out its client mods; TODO: the pack manager plan is replaced by this

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
